      },
      "message": "Use pointer size in the frame layout instead of XLEN\n\nThis is motivated by RVY where the frame layout uses YLEN (2*XLEN) values\nto store the return address/frame pointer.\n\nIt is also technically a change for the RV64ILP32 ABI, but my understanding\nis that this change is actually a bug fix, since we are storing pointers.\n\nSplit out from https://github.com/riscv-non-isa/riscv-elf-psabi-doc/pull/499",
